{"type":"assistant","uuid":"7f940dab-8749-406d-9ac0-5637f856e7c9","session_id":"169843ef-3dc8-4cb2-bd3e-4654150a2c99","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"7f940dab-8749-406d-9ac0-5637f856e7c9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to fix a URL encoding bug in an Android project. Let me understand the bug first:\n\n1. The issue is with URL encoding in a \"Uri Parts\" module\n2. When a URL contains `%25` (which is a double-encoded `%`), the application doesn't handle it properly\n3. The expected behavior is that `%25E6%259D%25A5%25E6%25BA%2590` should decode to `来源` (Chinese characters)\n4. But instead, it's showing garbled characters like `æ�¥æº`\n\nThe issue is that `%25` is the URL-encoded form of `%`. So when you have `%25E6%259D%25A5`, it should:\n1. First decode `%25` → `%`, giving `%E6%9D%A5`\n2. Then decode `%E6%9D%A5` → `来`\n\nBut it seems like the app is double-decoding or mishandling the encoding. The `%25` gets decoded to `%`, but then the resulting `%E6` is being interpreted as a literal `%` followed by `E6`, which then gets interpreted as UTF-8 bytes incorrectly.\n\nActually, looking more carefully:\n- The URL has `prefill_%25E6%259D%25A5%25E6%25BA%2590` \n- `%25` decodes to `%`\n- So after one decode: `prefill_%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90`\n- After full decode: `prefill_来源`\n\nBut the actual result shows `prefill_æ�¥æº` which looks like the UTF-8 bytes of the Chinese characters were interpreted as Latin-1/ISO-8859-1:\n- `E6 9D A5` as Latin-1 = `æ` + control char + `¥`\n\n\n- `E6 BA 90` as Latin-1 = `æ` + control char + `º`\n\nSo the actual bug is that the double-encoded URL (`%25...`) is being decoded once (correctly turning `%25` into `%`), but then the resulting `%E6%9D%A5...` is NOT being decoded again, and instead the UTF-8 bytes are being treated as individual characters. The parameter name `prefill_%25E6%259D%25A5%25E6%25BA%2590` is likely being URL-decoded only once, which leaves the second level of encoding intact.\n\nWhen the URL is decoded once, `%25` becomes `%`, giving us `prefill_%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90`. The value `E5%B8%AE...` decodes to `帮助与反馈` correctly, but the parameter name isn't being decoded a second time to get `来源`. The root cause appears to be a UTF-8 decoding issue where the raw bytes are being mishandled—likely the application isn't properly decoding the percent-encoded parameter name, or it's decoding it incorrectly. I should examine the URLCheck codebase, particularly the \"Uri Parts\" module, to see how URL parameters are being processed and where the encoding is failing.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
