{"type":"assistant","uuid":"4901b8c5-084e-4e8c-af1a-7036476ab8fa","session_id":"169843ef-3dc8-4cb2-bd3e-4654150a2c99","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"4901b8c5-084e-4e8c-af1a-7036476ab8fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build is successful. Here's a summary of the bug fix:\n\n## Bug Summary\n\n**Bug:** URL encoding problem with the Uri Parts module — double-encoded `%25` sequences are not handled properly, causing garbled display of parameter names containing percent-encoded UTF-8 characters (e.g., Chinese characters).\n\n**Root Cause:** The `UriPartsModule` used `android.net.UrlQuerySanitizer` to parse query parameters. `UrlQuerySanitizer` performs only **single-pass** URL decoding via `URLDecoder.decode()`. For double-encoded sequences like `%25E6%259D%25A5` (where `%25` represents a literal `%`), single-pass decoding produces incorrect intermediate results that corrupt the displayed text.\n\n## Fix Applied to `UriPartsModule.java`\n\n1. **Removed dependency on `UrlQuerySanitizer`** — replaced with a custom query string parser.\n\n2. **Added double-decoding logic** — the new `decodeQueryParam()` method applies `URLDecoder.decode()` twice:\n   - First pass: `%25` → `%`, and other `%XX` → characters\n   - Second pass: remaining `%XX` sequences (including the decoded `%`) → actual characters\n\n3. **Example:** `prefill_%25E6%259D%25A5%25E6%25BA%2590`\n   - Before (broken): `prefill_æ¥æº` (garbled)\n   - After (fixed): `prefill_来源` (correct)\n\nThe patch file is at: `uriparts-double-decode.patch`"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":79252,"output_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":78144,"total_tokens":79619}}}
