{"type":"assistant","uuid":"9af810b7-2f4c-4b93-abe2-674edd70441d","session_id":"169843ef-3dc8-4cb2-bd3e-4654150a2c99","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"9af810b7-2f4c-4b93-abe2-674edd70441d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_895ab21edcc9492289c45cd1","name":"write_file","input":{"content":"---\nname: UriPartsModule double-encoding fix\ndescription: How to fix URL double-encoding (e.g. %25 in Chinese URLs) in the UriPartsModule of the UrlChecker Android app\ntype: feedback\n---\n\n**Bug:** `android.net.UrlQuerySanitizer` does single-pass URL decode, corrupting double-encoded query param names like `%25E6%259D%25A5` (which should decode to `来`).\n\n**Fix:** Replace `UrlQuerySanitizer` with a custom parser that applies `URLDecoder.decode()` twice on query param names and values:\n1. First pass: `%25` → `%`, other `%XX` → characters\n2. Second pass: remaining `%XX` sequences → actual characters\n\n**Why:** Double-encoded URLs (common with UTF-8 characters) have `%25` representing a literal `%`. Single-pass decode turns `%25E6%259D%25A5` into `%E6%9D%A5` (still percent-encoded), not `来`. Two passes resolve it fully.\n\n**How to apply:** In `UriPartsModule.java` `onDisplayUrl()`, replace `UrlQuerySanitizer` usage with `parseQueryParams()` which splits on `&`/`=` and calls `decodeQueryParam()` (double `URLDecoder.decode`).\n\n**Related files with same issue:** `RemoveQueriesModule.java`, `ClearUrlModule.java`, `PatternModule.java` all use single-pass `URLDecoder.decode()`. They may need the same fix if they display/query double-encoded params.\n","file_path":"/home/antu_shared/.qwen/projects/-home-antu-shared-automated-program-repair-for-ui-bugs/memory/feedback/uriparts-double-decode.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":70400,"output_tokens":473,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"total_tokens":70873}}}
